<doc id="194977" url="https://jv.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=194977" title="Mohamed Ahmed Nassar">
Mohamed Ahmed Nassar

Mohamed Nassar is a journalist specializing in digital media. His practical experience extends to more than 15 years in the field of visual, print and electronic media.
He currently holds the positions of editor-in-chief of the Arabic version of Robb Report Arabia magazine and website, and the designated editor in chief of Al Rijal magazine and website, affiliated with the Saudi Research Group. And marketing.
<h2>Education</h2>
Education.
He obtained a bachelor’s degree in media in 2004 from the University of Damascus, and he also obtained a master’s degree in marketing in 2006 from the same university.
<h2>Professional Biography</h2>
Professional Biography.
Nassar began his career as a broadcaster on the Syrian news channel Sham Satellite for 3 years, extending from 2005 to 2008 AD, before moving to the Emirates and working as a presenter for the “Press” program on the “Al Sharqiya” channel, which broadcasts from Dubai, during the period from 2008 to 2015. He also worked as an editor in Al Sharq Al-Awsat newspaper in 20017 before being promoted to the position of director of the newspaper’s office in the Emirates, in addition to supervising a number of other files in the newspaper and conducting many interviews and press reports, including an interview with the regional director of “Shell Aviation” - director of Dubai Industrial City - CEO of ASDA’A Burson Marsteller.
Mohamed Nassar moved to the prestigious Al Rijal magazine, which was founded in 1992 and is based in London, and was appointed to the position of managing editor to establish the magazine’s website in 2013, before a decision was issued to appoint him as editor-in-chief at the end of 2020.
By 2017, Nassar was appointed to the position of managing editor of the youth lifestyle website Sidi, which is the men’s version of Sayidaty magazine.
In May 2021, Mohamed Nassar was appointed editor in chief of the website and magazine of the Arabic version of Rob Robert Report Arabia, which is based in the Production City in Dubai, in parallel with the presidency of both the “The Man” and “Sidi” editions.
<h2>Social Media Initiatives</h2>
Social Media Initiatives.
Mohamed Nassar launched the Distinguished Ten Award through Al Rajal magazine and website to highlight and honor those distinguished in a number of fields, after conducting a public vote on social media platforms to choose the most deserving of the award. Among the most famous winners of the competition are the 10 distinguished in managing Saudi clubs, and the 10 distinguished in inspiring Saudis., the top ten brands.
<h2>Social Responsibility</h2>
Social Responsibility.
Through his social media platforms, Nassar periodically publishes free cultural awareness content through the Leave a Trace program on his YouTube channel, and his account on the Twitter and Facebook platforms. He also provides rich content for self development through his website.
